  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\nCorrigendum\n\nCorrigendum to \"Midwifery continuity of carer in an area of high socioeconomic disadvantage in London: A retrospective analysis of Albany Midwifery Practice outcomes using routine data (1997-2009)\" [Midwifery 48 (2017) 1-10]\n\nCaroline S.E. Homer, RM, MMed(ClinEpi), PhD Professor Nicky Leap, DMid Adjunct Professor of Midwifery Nadine Edwards, PhD Independent Researcher ,,c , Jane Sandall, PhD; CBE Professor, NIHR Senior Investigator ,c\n\nCentre for Midwifery, Child and Family Health, Faculty of Health, University of Technology Sydney, PO Box 123, Broadway, Sydney; New South Wales 2007, Australia\n\nWomen's Health Academic Centre, St. Thomas' Hospital, London SEI 7EH, United Kingdom\n\nDivision of Women's Health, Faculty of Life Sciences &amp;  Medicine, King's College London, United Kingdom\n\nThe authors regret that on page 8 we inadvertently referred to NICE as providing policy and policy direction: This was incorrect. NICE provides national clinical guidance based on systematic reviews. The sentence should read: A study comparing perinatal outcomes by planned place of birth (Birthplace in England Collaborative Group; 2011) supported the clinical guidance to offer women with low risk pregnancies a choice of birth settings; including birth at home (NICE, 2014). large\n\nThe authors would like to apologise for any inconvenience caused.\n\nDOI of original article:   http:/ /dx.doiorg/10.1016/j.midw.2017.02.009\n\nE-mail address: caroline @uts edu.au (CSE. Homer). homer(\n\nCorresponding author.\n\n[http: / /dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw. 2017.05.013](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013)\n\n0266-6138/ 2017 The Author(s). Published by Elsevier Ltd. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (http:/ /creativecommons org /licenses /BY-NC-ND/4.0/)\n\n## ARTICLE IN PRESS\n\n[Midwifery XXX (xxxx)](http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.midw.2017.05.013)\n\nContents lists available at ScienceDirect\n\n## Midwifery\n\njourna homepage: WWW elsevier comllocatelmidw\n\n<!-- image -->",
